WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.292
- [Voiceover] We put the power

00:00:02.292 --> 00:00:05.432
in PowerPoint today, right?
(laughter)

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:06.564
Yeah, for sure.

00:00:06.564 --> 00:00:10.206
- Hey guys, don't forget,
party this weekend, my place,

00:00:10.206 --> 00:00:14.432
bring booze, chips and most
importantly yourselves.

00:00:14.432 --> 00:00:18.112
- Oh, I can't make it on Friday.

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:21.467
I agreed to help a friend move,

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.106
and I don't know what time
we're going to be done.

00:00:24.106 --> 00:00:26.947
- Yeah, I wish I could go
too, but my dad's in town

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:28.746
and I got to show him around the old city.

00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:29.876
You know how dads are.

00:00:29.876 --> 00:00:31.006
- [Man in Jacket] Dads love cities.

00:00:31.006 --> 00:00:32.137
- They love cities, true.

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:34.713
- Well bummer, well
what about you, Quinta?

00:00:34.713 --> 00:00:39.285
- Oh, uh, I can't go either
because I don't want to, sorry.

00:00:41.284 --> 00:00:46.284
- Um, I'm sorry? Do you
have something to do?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.451
- Uh, no, I just don't want to go.

00:00:51.158 --> 00:00:53.195
- Do you, uh, is your dad in town?

00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:54.796
And you have to take
him around the city too?

00:00:54.796 --> 00:00:58.229
- Oh no no no, my dad is living
peacefully in Philadelphia.

00:00:58.229 --> 00:00:59.684
He hasn't visited in years.

00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:00.528
I just don't want to go.

00:01:00.528 --> 00:01:04.675
- You don't want to go
because it's far away.

00:01:04.675 --> 00:01:06.573
Because it's in Studio
City and that's a drive.

00:01:06.573 --> 00:01:09.219
- I actually live pretty close
to Studio City in The Valley.

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:12.021
Yeah, I just don't want
to attend the party.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.323
- I'm sorry, Quinta.
Is it something I did?

00:01:17.323 --> 00:01:19.459
- Oh my God, Justin,
no, are you kidding me?

00:01:19.459 --> 00:01:21.282
You're a dear, you didn't do anything.

00:01:21.282 --> 00:01:23.523
I just would rather not, and will not,

00:01:23.523 --> 00:01:24.487
be attending your party.

00:01:26.645 --> 00:01:28.050
- Hold on, is it because you have

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:29.736
an improv class that night?

00:01:29.736 --> 00:01:31.472
That's what it is.

00:01:31.472 --> 00:01:34.421
- No, that's actually at three
o'clock PM, in the afternoon.

00:01:34.421 --> 00:01:37.117
- Oh but that night
you've got roller derby.

00:01:37.117 --> 00:01:38.592
That's why you can't go.

00:01:38.592 --> 00:01:41.155
- Thank you so much for
remembering Steve, such a doll.

00:01:41.155 --> 00:01:43.502
But that actually got
cancelled this weekend.

00:01:43.502 --> 00:01:44.170
- Quinta, let me get this straight.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.328
- Yeah.

00:01:45.328 --> 00:01:48.606
- I'm having a party,
and you're my friend ...

00:01:48.606 --> 00:01:49.838
- I am.

00:01:49.838 --> 00:01:52.718
- And I invited you.
- Thank you.

00:01:52.718 --> 00:01:53.743
- But ...

00:01:53.743 --> 00:01:55.846
- I am not going to that party.

00:01:55.846 --> 00:01:57.411
- What are you going to do instead?

00:01:57.411 --> 00:02:00.101
- What is your reason for
not going to his party?

00:02:00.101 --> 00:02:01.220
- Oh my reason.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:04.000
The reason that I am not
going to Justin's party,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.055
is that I do not want
to go to Justin's party.

00:02:07.055 --> 00:02:08.889
- Hold on. Let's figure this out.

00:02:09.905 --> 00:02:11.533
I invited you to a party ...
- [Quinta] Yes.

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:15.663
- Which mean Quinta goes, right?

00:02:15.663 --> 00:02:17.619
- Okay, let me show you the
problem with your logic there.

00:02:17.619 --> 00:02:19.918
Let me get that, math's just a little off.

00:02:19.918 --> 00:02:22.237
So, see what you did here?

00:02:22.237 --> 00:02:24.556
But what you forgot was X.

00:02:24.556 --> 00:02:26.877
Which is I don't want to go.

00:02:26.877 --> 00:02:29.937
Which then changes the
outcome to I am not going.

00:02:29.937 --> 00:02:32.817
- Wait, what?
- It's simple math.

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:36.972
- I get it, Quinta here is
trying to pull a fast one on us.

00:02:36.972 --> 00:02:38.911
She's saying that she's not going to go,

00:02:38.911 --> 00:02:40.350
she's going to show up
halfway through the party

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.893
and yell surprise, it's an
opposite surprise party.

00:02:42.893 --> 00:02:45.494
(laughter)
- Oh, that's genius.

00:02:45.494 --> 00:02:47.688
- That is a really fun way
to think of it you guys,

00:02:47.688 --> 00:02:50.810
if the surprise is that
I will not be there,

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.705
because I'm not going.

00:02:51.705 --> 00:02:55.405
- Come on, I'm having a
party, and I invited you,

00:02:55.405 --> 00:02:56.354
and you're just not going to go

00:02:56.354 --> 00:02:58.524
because you don't want to go?

00:02:58.524 --> 00:03:01.684
At least these guys came
up with valid excuses.

00:03:05.927 --> 00:03:07.943
Right guys? Steve?

00:03:11.164 --> 00:03:13.105
- I wish I could be as honest as Quinta.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.534
I'm not going because I don't want to go.

00:03:21.183 --> 00:03:22.843
- I mean my dad actually is in town,

00:03:22.843 --> 00:03:24.816
and wants to go see the city, but I mean,

00:03:24.816 --> 00:03:26.637
if he wants to go to
your party then maybe.

00:03:26.637 --> 00:03:27.486
- Hello Son.

00:03:27.486 --> 00:03:31.618
- Oh hey sir, would you be
interested in coming to my party?

00:03:31.618 --> 00:03:33.137
- No, I don't want to go to your party.

00:03:33.137 --> 00:03:37.952
(techno music)

